<!--
  The mark Animato wears in the status bar.

  A notification's small icon is not a logo slot: Android throws away every colour in it and draws
  the alpha channel in whatever tint the system is using, at roughly 24dp inside a 22dp keyline.
  The app icon cannot be used here — its panel, its cream ground and its two words survive that
  treatment as an illegible grey smudge — which is why this is a separate, deliberately blunt
  shape rather than a reference to the launcher icon.

  So it draws the one thing the brand is recognisable by at that size: the leaning A of the
  wordmark, cut from a rounded panel the way the icon's letters are cut from theirs. Solid white
  on transparent, no strokes thinner than the keyline, nothing that depends on colour to read.

  It replaced `ic_ani`, the donor app's ring-and-triangle, which was still appearing on every
  Animato notification.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24">
    <!--
      The panel: a rounded rectangle with a corner clipped away, echoing the tilted comic frame the
      launcher icon is built on. Drawn as an outline so the letter inside stays legible when the
      whole thing is tinted one flat colour.
    -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:pathData="M4,2.6h16c0.77,0 1.4,0.63 1.4,1.4v16c0,0.77 -0.63,1.4 -1.4,1.4H4c-0.77,0 -1.4,-0.63 -1.4,-1.4V4c0,-0.77 0.63,-1.4 1.4,-1.4zM4.6,4.6v14.8h14.8V4.6z" />
    <!--
      The A, leaning the way the wordmark's letters lean. The crossbar is a full-width block rather
      than a hairline so it survives being drawn at status-bar size.
    -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:pathData="M11.1,6.6h2.2l3.5,10.8h-2.3l-0.66,-2.2h-3.9l-0.66,2.2h-2.3zM12,9.3l-1.2,4h2.5z" />
</vector>
